{
  "check_id": "W7B8:W7B8:CHK-0051",
  "title": "Supporting Check: Does the request-response client enforce count * NUMBER_OF_COLUMNS response limit?",
  "severity": "Medium",
  "test_procedure": "1. Identify the actor-req-resp-client component and its DataColumnSidecarsByRange response parsing logic. 2. Verify the client calculates the expected maximum: count * NUMBER_OF_COLUMNS. 3. Test client behavior when receiving responses with: (a) exactly count * NUMBER_OF_COLUMNS sidecars - should accept, (b) count * NUMBER_OF_COLUMNS + 1 sidecars - should reject/truncate, (c) MAX_REQUEST_DATA_COLUMN_SIDECARS sidecars when count * NUMBER_OF_COLUMNS is smaller - should reject. 4. Verify the client stores the 'count' from the original request to validate response size. 5. Check for time-of-check-time-of-use issues where count could be modified between request and response validation. 6. Verify memory allocation uses the stricter limit to prevent oversized buffer allocation. 7. Test that peers sending oversized responses are penalized appropriately.",
  "code_excerpt": "// From beacon-chain/sync/rpc_send_request.go:457-570 - SendDataColumnSidecarsByRangeRequest
// The client enforces: totalCount = request.Count * columnsCount (line ~470)
// And checks totalCount > maxRequestDataColumnSidecars (line ~472)
// The read loop iterates 'for range totalCount' (line ~520) - this is count*len(columns), not count*NUMBER_OF_COLUMNS
// After reading all expected, it does an extra read expecting EOF (line ~558)
// If not EOF, returns errMaxResponseDataColumnSidecarsExceeded and downscores peer

func SendDataColumnSidecarsByRangeRequest(
	p DataColumnSidecarsParams,
